# Open this file in Visual Studio 2022 or VS Code (REST Client extension) and click "Send Request".
# Use the port printed by `dotnet run` (usually 5000 or 5xxx).
@host = http://localhost:5000

### 1. Health check
GET {{host}}/

### 2. First weigh: loaded truck arrives (gross)
POST {{host}}/weighings
Content-Type: application/json

{ "registration": "CA 123-456", "product": "Wheat", "grossKg": 34560 }

### 3. Validation: tare heavier than gross should be rejected (400). Change 1 to the id returned above.
POST {{host}}/weighings/1/second
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tareKg": 99999 }

### 4. Second weigh: truck leaves empty (tare). Same id as above.
POST {{host}}/weighings/1/second
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tareKg": 14200 }

### 5. Look up the ticket (nett is now filled in)
GET {{host}}/weighings/1

### 6. Today's report (JSON)
GET {{host}}/reports/daily

### 7. Today's report as CSV (opens in Excel)
GET {{host}}/reports/daily.csv
